From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:36:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Run in WebKit, and survive a host stack overflow

Do not use `using` in the package source: it compiles to helpers that
call Symbol.dispose at run time, which WebKit (Safari, WKWebView) does not
define, so every JSException failed. Define Symbol.dispose and
Symbol.asyncDispose when missing, before the classes that key methods by them.

When a call out of WASM throws something other than through the wrapper's
guest-exception path (the host's stack overflowed, or the code trapped),
its frames were unwound without cleanup and __stack_pointer stayed lowered
for the whole instance. Restore it, and retire the VM that was running:
every later call on it throws.
---
 src/index.ts         | 175 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 test/dispose.test.ts |  12 +++
 test/stack.test.ts   |  32 ++++++++
 3 files changed, 176 insertions(+), 43 deletions(-)

